Description:

JMAP vCard blobIds now encode the content identifier of the card they name.
Previously a blobId encoded only the containing mailbox and the record number
within it, so a blobId could be constructed rather than obtained from the
server, and one continued to resolve after the record it named had been
replaced by different content.  This is a breaking change: blobIds issued by
earlier versions are rejected, and a client holding one must ask for a
current blobId.

Tracked as GitHub security advisory GHSA-gvph-c6cq-j8xc.


